---Resolve commit shas to commit list rows
---
---Resolves a batch of commit shas to rows with the same shape the commits list serves, including embedded checkpoint previews with resolved session names. The map is keyed by each sha exactly as requested; the row's own commitSha is the canonical lowercase form and may differ in case from its key — join on the key, not the row field. Unknown, garbage-collected, and malformed shas are absent from the map, so callers keep whatever fallback they already hold. Diff stats come from the same git computation the commits list serves (first-parent diff); a commit whose diff missed entiredb's per-commit budget carries null stats, exactly like the list. Checkpoint preview placement follows the requested sha set — a checkpoint anchors to its latest linking commit within the set — so a commit's previews can differ from the list page's placement. Built for search-result hydration: the search index stores only index-time text, and this read overlays live row data at query time.
---
---`POST /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}/commits:resolve-rows`
---@param input entire.code.ResolveRepoCommitRowsRequest
---@return entire.code.CommitRowsResolveOutputBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
